l temple from ocarina of time and  sure it may have just been kept up with  all these years but how can it be the  same one if it's so far from the castle  you ask  well actually if you're interested in my  full theory that a lot of these land  masses may have shifted around in breath  of the wild's hyrule check out the  theory i did with nintendo black crisis  on hyrule's moving castle i'll link to  it in the description below anyway i  tend to believe that when you have  literal landmarks or land masses that  are giant  similarities or direct references to  previous zelda games they're probably  the real deal  like death mountain i don't think there  are multiple death mountains  i'm pretty sure that one there is the  only one that's ever been  so using my own sort of criteria for  what it is and is not canon in the game  what about this statue of darmani canon  or non-canon and  for those who are unfamiliar with who  darmani is i'll summarize real quick  in the rather dark and depressing game  majora's mask link travels to the  mysterious land of termina  and there meets several key characters  who are all either dead or  dying so that he can get masks from them  and use their powers to complete the  temples of the game  good stuff good stuff but one of these  dying characters is the beloved goron  hero darmani who link finds as already  having died  but struggling with the fact so link  ends up healing darmani's soul with the  song of healing which allows him to  accept his death and move on  and then link is able to grab darmani's  freshly made goron mask  all well and good but that happened  within the land of termina  and this statue here is in hyrule so  canon or non-canon  i say it's canon because it's not the  only statue in goron city  there's also daruk from this very game  who i'm pretty sure  is canon and the goron elder from  twilight princess who is definitely a  part of hyrule's history  carved into the very map of breath of  the wild  so logically 