lly  removed from hyrule by some great  distance  yes that's exactly what i'm saying now  to prove it  let's take a look at how link enters  termina yes it's a trippy fall down a  hollowed-out tree that feels very much  like a portal but that's just it  i do believe it is a portal that's no  different than the other portals already  present in the woods  look the lost woods is a magical place  where people can literally  infinitely get turned around and around  and around  until they're lost forever and even  sometimes turn into monsters and it's  also a place where literal magical  portals link to places like goron city  and zora's domain  so why not also a portal that links to  termina a place  just as physically real as goron city or  zora's domain and as far as the theory  that termina is not physically real and  simply a creation of the power of majora  how then does it still exist after  majora's defeat and removal of power  at the end of the game shouldn't the  world have immediately crumbled into  non-existence like coho lint island did  when the wind fish woke up  there are even some evidences of  possible majora influence bleeding over  into hyrule's history like the  well-known eyes on midna's fused shadow  helmet thing or twilight princess  ganondorf's original armor design  these design choices have led many to  believe that the creators of the fused  shadow  also known as the interlopers and the  ancient tribe that created the majora's  mask could possibly be one and the same  and i'm not gonna go into that anymore  but if that's true it would obviously  mean termina is a real place  accessible from the lost woods  furthermore in a land that features  no landmarks from hyrule why would a  goron directly reference  hyrule's dadango's cavern from ocarina  of time unless they do  exist in the same world and that's the  actual dodongo's cavern they're  referencing  the final piece of evidence for terminus  existence is  the dharmani sculpture since it's made  from the minds of gorons and gorons are  canon  that has to mean that not only is  termina an actual real place  but the gorons from termina either in  part or holy came  over at some point to join their  hyrulian brothers maybe they even came  through the lost woods portals who knows  and when they arrived  their histories and legends now became  one and the same  either way i believe that's the story  behind this statue  i believe it proves that termina is a  real  place and that is just my theory but  what did you guys think you think i'm  onto something or is this literally a  non-canon piece of rock that doesn't  actually exist  let me know in the comments below thank  you all so much for watching  i really hope you enjoyed the video if  you did please consider subscribing to  help the channel grow and leaving a like  to help the video grow as always  huge thanks goes to all of my amazing  supporters introducing  several new names say hello to justin l  josh  a puppet of fate luna hellweg and  michael g  who all decided to become my elite crew  and support the channel  if you're interested in getting your  name up here at the end of each of my  videos and helping my next video come to  life  check out that join button located below  this video or the links in the  description below  also down there are of course the links  to my social media pages so hey  come connect with me and say hi on  twitter this is maskingtonabandit  signing out and hoping that you have a  great rest of your day peace  [Music]  you

